1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
From one task to a table and inspectable outputs.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Codex reaches RStudio through MCP; this demo uses synthetic data only.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:29,500
Start the named demo session in the ClaudeR addin.

4
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:37,500
Discover sessions, then connect explicitly to demo.

5
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:45,500
Check R and ClaudeR versions, sample size and IDs.

6
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:53,500
Hash the input, read the dataset and inspect its structure.

7
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:58,500
Group counts are 704 and 496; missing values and duplicate IDs are reported.

8
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:08,500
Education has 24 missing values; health has 36; duplicate IDs: zero.

9
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:20,500
The specification defines groups, summary methods and missing categories.

10
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:30,500
The background task returns a job ID; subsequent checks use that same ID.

11
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:40,500
This is the actual submission; the console remains available during computation.

12
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:50,500
The run produces DOCX, CSV, RDS, metadata and a hash manifest.

13
00:01:50,500 --> 00:02:00,500
This view is rendered from the newly generated DOCX; values are not retyped.

14
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:08,500
Bilingual labels, group summaries and test results remain editable.

15
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:16,500
Missing categories are retained; the three-line table has no vertical grid.

16
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:26,500
Reopen the outputs and check numeric values, display values and hashes.

17
00:02:26,500 --> 00:02:39,500
All six checks are TRUE; the input SHA-256 is unchanged.

18
00:02:39,500 --> 00:02:49,500
Validation covers document structure, value consistency and input integrity.

19
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:57,500
Behind the footage are four real Codex MCP calls; times come from its session log.

20
00:02:57,500 --> 00:03:07,500
Follow the README to install compatible versions and connect your named session.

21
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:15,500
Built on IMNMV/ClaudeR; a synthetic-data demo with retained outputs.
